    "explanation": {
      "event_selection": "Events are restricted to essential controllable mission decisions (search_object, claim_<color>, approach_object, pick_up_object, search_zone, approach_zone, drop_object) and mandatory color- and zone-related uncontrollable observations for ordered box search, claim arbitration, pickup, and delivery. Low-level movement and obstacle/collision events are omitted as these are managed by fixed specifications.",
      "transition_design": "Transitions enforce a deterministic, nonblocking delivery flow: begin searching for any color; after <color>_object_visible, enter claim attempt; a successful claim_<color> commits to that color branch, while a received_claim_<color> reverts to the initial search; approach_object and reacquisition with proper reacquire object search are explicitly modeled for recovery. Object_reached can advance from both approach and reacquire, securing resilience. Pickup enables searching for, and approaching, the matching zone, with symmetric reacquisition. Drop occurs only at zone_reached, marking completion. Branches for red, green, and blue ensure unique color assignment per robot.",
      "feedback_response": "This revision remains faithful to the control objective by focusing exclusively on single-delivery-per-robot, unique-claim, and full action-observation coverage for every indicated mission stage. The reacquire phases after loss of object or zone visibility remain explicit, directly addressing previous feedback on stalls during search or approach. Self-loops for actions such as search_object, approach_object, and search_zone allow repetition until success and support recovery, thereby increasing mission completeness and eliminating bottlenecks exposed by the prior run."
